e and i have some confidence we're  going to get it done  no i'm very impressed with the problem  solvers caucus because you try to put  politics aside and at least find some  common ground it looks like enough has  been found here that you have  so uh congressman johnson to you on that  um  do you think there is enough common  ground that this will pass  i absolutely think it's going to pass it  needs to pass  the reality is 778 000 americans filed  for unemployment for the first time last  week  and we had 10 000 of our countrymen die  and i think neil you see  that every hour that goes by another  prominent legislative leader steps up  and adds their voice to ours frankly  this thing looked dead a week ago  but since we made our announcement on  tuesday all of the momentum  is headed toward passage  joe biden has offered some insight in  his thinking on this and i think  congressman phillips what he was saying  is  he'd like to see that 1200 stimulus  check that that was obviously  very popular the initial pandemic relief  plan  uh i don't believe it's part of this one  yet  uh do you think it will be you know neil  time will tell of course the president  uh was very much in favor of direct  stimulus checks in the past  you know i believe that consumption is  the engine of the economy and money in  people's pockets  is the fuel and in times like these i do  believe that sending money to people  directly who are struggling the most  is a net benefit to the economy actually  will cost less now than it will down the  road so i am in favor of it  uh we weren't able to achieve everything  that everybody wanted in the current  framework but i'm still hopeful that  that could  if it finds bipartisan support could be  achieved because i certainly favor it  um congressman johnson i talked to your  republican counterpart in the senate  chuck grassley  who was saying um you know he's open to  this he's open to a lot of it but don't  go  crazy on on you know another effort t